   pseudocomplements in some lattices of module classes. The classes of
   modules belonging to these lattices are defined via closure under
   operations such as taking submodules, quotients, extensions, injective
   hulls, direct sums or products. We characterize the rings for which the
   lattices R-tors (of hereditary torsion classes), R-nat (the lattice of
   natural classes) and R-conat (the lattice of conatural classes)
   coincide.},
