   Irsee, GERMANY, JUL 04-08, 2018},
Organization = {OReilly; DPunkt; Hillside Europe e V},
Abstract = {The Architectural Patterns for Parallel Programming is a collection of
   patterns related with a method for developing the coordination structure
   of parallel software systems. These architectural patterns take as input
   information (a) the available parallel hardware platform, (b) the
   parallel programming language of this platform, and (c) the analysis of
   the problem to solve, in terms of an algorithm and data. In this paper,
   it is presented the application of the architectural patterns along
   within the Coordination stage, as part of the Pattern -based Parallel
   Software Design Method, which aims for developing a coordination
   structure for solving the Laplace Equation. The Coordination stage here
   takes the information from the Problem Analysis presented in Section 2,
   selects an architectural pattern for the coordination in Section 3, and
   provides some elements about its implementationin Section 4.},
