   Perspectives on the Reception and Production of the Comic Phenomenon},
Booktitle = {PSYCHOLOGY AND PHYLOSOPHY OF HUMOR},
Series = {Humor-Aproximaciones Transdisciplinares},
Year = {2018},
Pages = {31-88},
Abstract = {The phenomenon of the comic will be studied based on the historical
   analysis of the concept of popular culture and its aesthetic and
   critical reception, the question about the limits of the body category,
   and the feasibility of a hermeneutics of laughter from the context of
   European popular culture. For this purpose, we will review the tacit
   debate between two authors: Theodor Lipps and Mikhail M. Bakhtin, the
   first one from the perspective of a psychology of humor and the second
   one from the problematic view of popular culture in the Middle Ages and
   the Renaissance.},
